=== start ===
# You encounter the NPC near a community board with a poster about the oil drilling project.

#speaker: Player  
Hey, saw that poster about the drilling project? They're pushing it as a big win, but there’s more to it than they’re letting on.

* [The facts don’t add up. How can we ignore the long-term damage to the environment?] -> logical_tone
* [It’s heartbreaking. They’re selling this as progress, but it could ruin everything we’ve worked for.] -> emotional_tone
* [Think about it. Why would they rush this project unless there was something they didn’t want us to notice?] -> argumentative_tone
* [I get it—it’s a complicated issue. Maybe we should take some time to really think it over.] -> reserved_tone

=== logical_tone ===
#speaker: Player  
The facts don’t add up. How can we ignore the long-term damage to the environment? The science is clear—drilling like this will have devastating effects.

#speaker: other  
I don’t know. Energy independence sounds important. If we don’t act now, we might lose our edge.

* [True, but there are better ways to achieve energy independence without risking the planet.] -> logical_tone
* [Doesn’t it worry you what this will do to the ecosystems around the drilling sites?] -> emotional_tone
* [That’s what they want us to think. But why is no one talking about the environmental costs?] -> argumentative_tone
* [I’m not here to debate, just to help us think about all the angles.] -> reserved_tone

=== emotional_tone ===
#speaker: Player  
It’s heartbreaking. They’re selling this as progress, but it could ruin everything we’ve worked for. The forests, the rivers—they might never recover.

#speaker: other  
I see your point, but energy is a necessity. What if we have no choice?

* [We always have a choice. Renewable energy could achieve the same goals without the destruction.] -> logical_tone
* [Think about how the local communities will suffer. People’s homes and livelihoods are at risk.] -> emotional_tone
* [This feels like another case of profits over people. Why else would they ignore these consequences?] -> argumentative_tone
* [Maybe you're right, but let’s take a moment to dig deeper before deciding.] -> reserved_tone

=== argumentative_tone ===
#speaker: Player  
Think about it. Why would they rush this project unless there was something they didn’t want us to notice? This isn’t just about energy—it’s about control and profits.

#speaker: other  
It’s hard to say. But without these resources, aren’t we vulnerable to outside pressures?

* [Not if we invest in sustainable energy solutions. We’d be independent and environmentally responsible.] -> logical_tone
* [Maybe, but wouldn’t you feel more secure knowing we’re not destroying our future in the process?] -> emotional_tone
* [That’s exactly what they want us to believe. But it’s a trap to keep us dependent on destructive methods.] -> argumentative_tone
* [You might be right. Let’s take this step by step and learn more before jumping to conclusions.] -> reserved_tone

=== reserved_tone ===
#speaker: Player  
I get it—it’s a complicated issue. Maybe we should take some time to really think it over. Rushing won’t help anyone.

#speaker: other  
I agree. It’s worth considering all sides before we make up our minds.

* [Exactly. The truth will always reveal itself if we’re willing to look for it.] -> logical_tone
* [I hope you’ll see that this project could cost us more than it gives. It’s about our legacy.] -> emotional_tone
* [We can’t blindly trust their motives. Let’s make sure we’re not being misled.] -> argumentative_tone
* [I’ll leave you to think it through. Let me know if you want to talk more.] -> reserved_tone
